I didn't realize there was another dependency that doesn't get packed: as part of the rebuild process it needs the source files for node itself. Assuming you are running Node 0.8.18 on your Ubuntu box, you should be able to find it at ~/.node-gyp/0.8.18. <http://0.8.18.> Copy that directory to the same location in the home directory on the Red Hat box. Once shiny-server is successfully installed you can delete it, I believe.

